    Mount cluster storage to your local filesystem via SSHFS.
    Enables native copy-paste (Ctrl+C / Ctrl+V), drag-and-drop, and local editing.
    Options:
      -d, --dir DIR      Remote path to mount (default: remote home directory)
      -m, --mount PATH   Local mount directory (default: ${MOUNT_POINT})
      -b, --browse       Open file manager (Dolphin/Nautilus) immediately after mounting

  cluster unmount [PATH]
    Safely detach the mounted cluster filesystem.

  cluster jupyter [OPTIONS]
    Launch remote JupyterLab with automatic port forwarding and browser opening.
    Options:
      -s, --slurm        Run on an allocated Slurm compute node
